# Shared data models

A type used by more than one part of the app lives in `src/data/` as a TypeScript model. Do not copy the same shape into a component, system, or util.

- One domain per file: `src/data/pokemon.ts`, `src/data/move.ts`.
- Export `type` aliases. This project uses `erasableSyntaxOnly`, so do not use `enum` or other syntax that emits runtime code. Model closed sets as string unions.
- Import models with `import type` and a `.ts` extension (`verbatimModuleSyntax`, `allowImportingTsExtensions`).
- A type used by only one component stays next to that component (for example its props type). Move it into `src/data/` as soon as a second module needs it.

```ts
// src/data/pokemon.ts
export type PokemonId = string

export type PokemonType = 'fire' | 'water' | 'grass'

export type Pokemon = {
  id: PokemonId
  name: string
  types: readonly PokemonType[]
}
```

```ts
// src/components/PokemonCard/PokemonCard.tsx
import type { Pokemon, PokemonId } from '../../data/pokemon.ts'
```

```ts
// ❌ BAD — a second copy of the shape inside a gameplay module
type Pokemon = { id: string; name: string }
```
